---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.PatchCuratorsCuratedPackagesRequest
---@field accessSettings? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.AccessControlSettings Required. Settings for controlling access to the curated package. Access to this curated package is limited to the allowlisted media planners and the creator. Buyers and bidders can not be allowlisted for or have direct access to this resource.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the curated package was created. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the curated package was last updated. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field curationFeeVisibility? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.CuratedPackageCurationFeeVisibilityEnum|string Optional. Immutable. The visibility of the combined curation package fee and data segment fees (the total curation fee).
---@field feeCpm? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.Money Optional. The CPM fee charged by the curator to buyers using this curated package. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field millipercentOfMediaFee? string Optional. The fee will be charged as a percentage of the impression cost, represented in millipercent. For example, 1% is represented as 1000.
---@field targeting? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.PackageTargeting Optional. Targeting criteria for the curated package.
---@field description? string Optional. A description of the curated package, provided by the curator.
---@field floorPriceCpm? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.Money Optional. The minimum CPM a buyer has to bid to participate in auctions for inventory in this curated package. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name assigned to the curated package by the curator. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.CuratedPackageStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the curated package. Can be used to filter the response of the curatedPackages.list method.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. List of fields to be updated. If empty or unspecified, the service will update all fields populated in the update request excluding the output only fields and primitive fields with default value. Note that explicit field mask is required in order to reset a primitive field back to its default value, for example, false for boolean fields, 0 for integer fields. A special field mask consisting of a single path "*" can be used to indicate full replacement (the equivalent of PUT method), updatable fields unset or unspecified in the input will be cleared or set to default value. Output only fields will be ignored regardless of the value of updateMask.
---@field name string Identifier. The unique resource name for the curated package. Format: `curators/{accountId}/curatedPackages/{curatedPackageId}`

---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.PatchCuratorsDataSegmentsRequest
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time the data segment was created.
---@field cpmFee? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.Money Optional. A fixed fee charged per thousand impressions. Once set, the currency code cannot be changed.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time the data segment was last updated.
---@field userListId? string Optional. Immutable. The ID of the User List wrapped by this Data Segment. Curators with a linked Data Partner account can create a data segment that wraps a user list owned by the linked Data Partner account. User lists can be uploaded and managed using the [Data Manager API](https://developers.google.com/data-manager/api/data-partners/audiences). Linking a user list to a data segment lets you define a segment of inventory that is based on an audience you create.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.DataSegmentStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the data segment.
---@field millipercentOfMediaFee? string Optional. The fee will be charged as a percentage of the impression cost, represented in millipercent. For example, 1% is represented as 1000.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The unique identifier for the data segment. Account ID corresponds to the account ID that created the segment. v1alpha format: `buyers/{accountId}/dataSegments/{curatorDataSegmentId}` v1beta format: `curators/{curatorAccountId}/dataSegments/{curatorDataSegmentId}`
---@field updateMask? string Optional. List of fields to be updated. If empty or unspecified, the service will update all fields populated in the update request excluding the output only fields and primitive fields with default value. Note that explicit field mask is required in order to reset a primitive field back to its default value, for example, false for boolean fields, 0 for integer fields. A special field mask consisting of a single path "*" can be used to indicate full replacement(the equivalent of PUT method), updatable fields unset or unspecified in the input will be cleared or set to default value. Output only fields will be ignored regardless of the value of updateMask.

---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.SearchMediaPlannersRequest
---@field dspSeatId? string Required. The DSP seat ID to search for. The DSP seat ID is provided by the media planner.
---@field pageSize? number Optional. The maximum number of media planners to return. If unspecified, at most 100 media planners will be returned. The maximum value is 500; values above 500 will be coerced to 500.
---@field pageToken? string Optional. A token identifying a page of results the server should return. This value is received from a previous `SearchMediaPlanners` call in `SearchMediaPlannersResponse.nextPageToken`.

---A response containing media planner account information from a search.
---@class gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.SearchMediaPlannersResponse
---@field mediaPlanners? gcp.unstable.authorizedbuyersmarketplace_v1beta.MediaPlannerList List of media planners matching the search criteria.
---@field nextPageToken? string A token which can be passed to a subsequent call to the `SearchMediaPlanners` method to retrieve the next page of results in SearchMediaPlannersRequest.pageToken.

